    ("What is Loop Tiling (Loop Blocking) and how does it accelerate matrix multiplication?", "Advanced", "Divides large multidimensional iteration spaces into smaller sub-matrix tiles that fit entirely inside CPU L1/L2 data cache, reducing cache capacity misses."),
    ("How do Compilers handle Calling Conventions (cdecl, System V AMD64 ABI, fastcall)?", "Intermediate", "Defines which CPU registers pass arguments (RDI, RSI, RDX, RCX, R8, R9), which registers are caller-saved vs callee-saved, and how stack frames are cleaned up."),
    ("What is Stack Smashing Protection (`-fstack-protector-strong`) and Stack Canaries?", "Beginner", "Inserts random canary value on stack before local variables; checks canary integrity before function return; aborts if buffer overflow overwrote canary."),
    ("How does Copy Propagation differ from Constant Propagation?", "Beginner", "Copy propagation replaces occurrences of variable $y$ with variable $x$ after assignment `y = x`; enables subsequent dead code elimination of $y$."),
    ("What is the difference between Static and Dynamic Type Checking?", "Beginner", "Static checks types at compile time before execution (catches bugs early, zero runtime overhead); Dynamic checks types at runtime during execution."),
    ("How do Compilers implement Virtual Function Tables (`vtables`) for dynamic dispatch?", "Intermediate", "Each class with virtual functions has an array of function pointers (`vtable`); objects contain a hidden pointer (`vptr`) to the vtable, resolved at runtime in 2 memory dereferences."),
    ("What is Intermediate Representation Three-Address Code (3AC)?", "Beginner", "Linearized IR format where each instruction has at most one operator and at most three operands (`x = y op z`), simplifying translation to assembly."),
