    ("What is Type-Based Alias Analysis (TBAA) in C/C++?", "Advanced", "Assumes pointers of incompatible types (e.g. `int*` and `float*`) cannot point to the same memory address (Strict Aliasing Rule), enabling reordering across pointer writes."),
